                "Each item names finding_id, exactly one absolute file_path or mapped FILE node_handle, the check row's observed witness, resolution and optional params from its params_schema; add_close requires a physical line start within the span section after the opener, or EOF. "
                "Malformed items and stale/unoffered/invalid choices fail only their own rows; noop/error/preview evidence is retained, while committed rows carry final findings for their affected ids and the acted-on finding under finding. "
                "Apply's aggregate findings describe each written file's final version, observed once after its writes; files without commits keep their planning evidence. Missing means stale, never repaired. Unique unchanged content+semantic witnesses rebind after line drift; "
                "identical members require the original file version or a newly listed choice, except that later items follow this request's own proved edits via U02 offset maps. "
                "Overlapping edit domains are collision rows before any write; other items execute in input order within each canonical file, re-reading and re-planning after each commit. "
